name modroman
category Package
revision 29803
shortdesc Write numbers in lower case roman numerals
relocated 1
longdesc This package provides only two macros viz. \modromannumeral
longdesc which writes the number given as argument in lower case roman
longdesc numeral with a 'j' instead of a 'i' as the final letter of
longdesc numbers greater than 1 and \modroman{MyCounter} which writes
longdesc the value of a counter in the same way. You use the first in
longdesc the same way as the TeX primitive \romannumeral and the second
longdesc as LaTeX command \roman. The default option is 'vpourv' with
longdesc which 5 is 'translated' as 'v' and option 'upourv' whith which
longdesc the same 5 is given as 'u'.
runfiles size=2
 RELOC/tex/latex/modroman/modroman.sty
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/modroman
